/**
 * Colorado Closings (24 classroom hours) — module question bank.
 *
 * THE SECOND COURSE AN OUT-OF-STATE BROKER CANNOT ESCAPE. C.R.S. § 12-10-203(4)(b) relieves an applicant
 * licensed as a broker in another jurisdiction of everything EXCEPT the Colorado contracts course and this
 * one. Rule 2.1.A.2.c fixes the floor: "Real Estate Closings: not less than 24 hours."
 *
 * TWO-THIRDS OF THIS COURSE IS THE EIGHT PROBLEMS. The Commission's outline, approved 6 June 1996,
 * allocates 1.0 + 2.0 + 4.0 + 1.0 + 16.0 = 24.0, with Topic V requiring "preparation of a MINIMUM OF EIGHT
 * (8) CLOSING PROBLEMS using a mix of cash, owner carry, assumptions (FHA, VA and conventional), new loans
 * (FHA, VA and conventional), and a closing involving a multi-family property. THREE PROBLEMS SHALL BE
 * USING SAMPLES OF PREPARED CONTRACTS." The engine records the eight separately and does not credit this
 * course without them. NO ITEM IN THIS BANK MAY SUGGEST THAT READING SUBSTITUTES FOR WORKING A PROBLEM.
 *
 * THE OUTLINE'S OWN EXAMINATION REQUIREMENT, in its own capitals: "ALL STUDENTS MUST SUCCESSFULLY COMPLETE
 * A WRITTEN EXAMINATION COVERING ALL MAJOR TOPIC AREAS OF THIS OUTLINE." The items here are not that
 * examination.
 *
 * RULE 6.19 CARRIES THIS COURSE, and it was read in full:
 *   (A) the broker who has established a brokerage relationship "WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR THE PROPER CLOSING
 *       OF THE TRANSACTION" — whoever conducts it — must ensure the consumer receives a closing statement
 *       that is "ACCURATE, COMPLETE AND DETAILED ... SIGNED BY THE BROKER", and must deliver closing
 *       statements and other closing documents to the firm "IMMEDIATELY FOLLOWING CLOSING".
 *   (B) a broker who PREPARES the documents is responsible for their accuracy and completeness.
 *   (C) the broker must review closing documents and attend closing OR BE REASONABLY AVAILABLE; a
 *       substitute designated by the firm assumes JOINT RESPONSIBILITY with the absent broker.
 *   (D) earnest money delivered as set forth in Rule 5.12.A.
 *   (E) GOOD FUNDS — no disbursement or authorization of disbursement until funds are received AND
 *       available for immediate withdrawal as a matter of right, or under an agreement with a financial
 *       institution whose contingencies are satisfied.
 *
 * Each module carries one applied item, five engagement items and five remediation items. The correct
 * answer is authored at index 0 and permuted deterministically per item id at delivery. The public delivery
 * path strips correctChoice and rationale, and a test proves it. The 80 percent engagement and 100 percent
 * applied thresholds are STATECOURSE STANDARDS.
 *
 * WHAT WAS NOT READ, AND WHICH THEREFORE APPEARS IN NO ITEM: RESPA; the non-resident seller withholding
 * statute and FIRPTA, both named by the outline at Topic I.D; C.R.S. § 38-35-125, cited by Rule 6.19.E;
 * §§ 12-10-217, 12-10-218, 12-10-219, 12-10-222 and 12-10-304; the Commission's Transaction File Checklist,
 * named by Rule 6.20; every Commission-approved form, including the contracts the three prepared-contract
 * problems require; Colorado's property tax, assessment and levy statutes; Colorado's entity, trust,
 * probate and recording statutes; the Colorado Common Interest Ownership Act; and the federal lead-based
 * paint regulations. EVERY FIGURE AND CONVENTION IN EVERY COMPUTATIONAL ITEM IS SUPPLIED INSIDE THE ITEM AS
 * A GIVEN, and no Colorado tax rate, assessment ratio, billing cycle or proration convention is stated.
 *
 * Course version 1.0 submission draft — NOT APPROVED. No Colorado qualifying education hours are available.
 */

